    <!-- Ghazghkull Mag Uruk Thraka (p134-135) - 430 pts -->
    <selectionEntry id="orks-dp09-0000-0001" name="Ghazghkull Mag Uruk Thraka" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="unit">
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink id="orks-dp09-0000-cl01" name="Primarch:" hidden="false" targetId="e031-3c2-e3f8-d40a" primary="true"/>
        <categoryLink id="orks-dp09-0000-cl02" name="Unit:" hidden="false" targetId="36c3-e85e-97cc-c503" primary="false"/>
        <categoryLink id="orks-dp09-0000-cl03" name="LoW &amp; Primarchs (25% Limit)" hidden="false" targetId="2eaf-32d6-9d1d-d906" primary="false"/>
        <categoryLink id="orks-dp09-0000-cl04" name="Prime-Ork Unit Type" hidden="false" targetId="orks-cat0-prmk-0001" primary="false"/>
      </categoryLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule id="orks-dp09-0000-r001" name="Warlord Trait: The Great Green Prophet" page="135" hidden="false">
          <description>If Ghazghkull is an army&apos;s Warlord, he must have the following Warlord Trait:
The Great Green Prophet: When Ghazghkull&apos;s controlling player declares a Waaagh!, Ghazghkull immediately regains one lost Wound and gains the Feel No Pain (4+) special rule until the end of the following turn. In addition, an army with Ghazghkull as its Warlord gains an additional Reaction in the opposing player&apos;s Assault phase as long as he has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="orks-dp09-0000-r002" name="Armour of Beasts" page="134" hidden="false">
          <description>The Armour of Beasts grants a 2+ armour save and a 4+ invulnerable save (which is further improved to a 3+ invulnerable save because of Ghazghkull&apos;s Cybork Body).</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="orks-dp09-0000-r003" name="Mork&apos;s Roar" page="134" hidden="false">
          <description>The first time Mork&apos;s Roar is fired each battle, the Storm of Dakka profile must be used. For the remainder of the battle after that, only the Ammo Chugger profile may be used. Mork&apos;s Roar is counted as an &apos;auto&apos; weapon for those rules that refer to such weapons.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="orks-dp09-0000-r004" name="Gork&apos;s Klaw" page="134" hidden="false">
          <description>Gork&apos;s Klaw is counted as a &apos;power&apos; weapon for those rules that refer to such weapons.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="orks-dp09-0000-r005" name="Vengeful Rampage" page="135" hidden="false">
          <description>If Makari, Bana Wava in the controlling player&apos;s army is destroyed, then until the end of the battle Ghazghkull&apos;s Attacks characteristic is increased by +2, his Weapon Skill characteristic is reduced by -2, and his unit must declare a charge against the closest enemy unit if his unit is unengaged and within 8&quot; of enemy units at the start of the Assault phase (if two or more units are equally distant, the controlling player selects the target(s) of the charge).
Additionally, if Makari was destroyed by an attack made by an enemy model, then Ghazghkull gains Hatred towards that model&apos;s unit until the end of the battle.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="orks-dp09-0000-r006" name="Goff is Da Best" page="135" hidden="false">
          <description>All Shooting Attacks made against Ghazghkull&apos;s unit suffer a modifier of -1 to the Strength of the attack. If Ghazghkull&apos;s controlling player declares a Waaagh!, then the same effect also applies to all other units with the Da Kolours (Black is Ded &apos;Ard) special rule until the end of the following turn.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink id="orks-dp09-0000-il01" name="Da Kolours (X)" hidden="false" targetId="orks-rule-kolo-0001" type="rule"/>
        <infoLink id="orks-dp09-0000-il02" name="Black Is Ded &apos;Ard" hidden="false" targetId="orks-rule-kolo-blk0" type="rule"/>
        <infoLink id="orks-dp09-0000-il03" name="Da Boss" hidden="false" targetId="orks-rule-dbos-0001" type="rule"/>
        <infoLink id="orks-dp09-0000-il04" name="&apos;Ere We Go!" hidden="false" targetId="orks-rule-ewgo-0001" type="rule"/>
        <infoLink id="orks-dp09-0000-il05" name="Preferred Enemy (X)" hidden="false" targetId="37ab-d4db-891a-de8c" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Preferred Enemy (Commissar Sebastian Yarrick)"/>
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
        <infoLink id="orks-dp09-0000-il06" name="The Waaagh!" hidden="false" targetId="orks-rule-wagh-0001" type="rule"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup id="orks-dp09-warg-0001" name="Ork Wargear" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true">
          <entryLinks>
            <entryLink id="orks-dp09-warg-el01" name="Stikkboms" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" targetId="orks-warg-stik-0001" type="selectionEntry">
              <constraints>
                <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-dp09-warg-c001" type="max"/>
              </constraints>
            </entryLink>
